-- title:
--   Tame inertia over q is cyclic modulo p^m-th powers
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ and $q$ be distinct primes, let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` such that $q$, viewed in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, is a non-unit of $P$ (this is the condition `P.LiesOverPrime q`, saying that $P$ is a place above $q$), and let $m$ be a natural number. Write $I_P \le \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ for `P.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup of $P$ into the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is that there exists $\gamma \in I_P$ with the property that every $\tau \in I_P$ admits a factorisation $\tau = \gamma^{j}\, x^{p^{m}}\, w^{p^{m}}$ for some natural number $j$ and some $x, w \in I_P$. Thus $I_P$ is generated by a single element together with $p^m$-th powers of its own elements; the conclusion is stated with two $p^m$-th power factors rather than one, and $\gamma$ is not claimed to be independent of $m$.
--
--   This records the standard structure of tame inertia at a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $q$: modulo the subgroup generated by $p^m$-th powers, the inertia group at $P$ is cyclic, generated by the image of a single tame generator. It is used in the local analysis of deformation conditions, where bounds on invariants and on the length of cotangent modules for representations that are unipotent on inertia at $q$ are obtained from the action of one generator.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_tame_generator_inertiaSubgroupIn.lean

